---

##### Variable definitions

- $x_{w,p} = 1$ if worker $w$ is assigned to project $p$, $0$ otherwise, for all eligible $(w,p)$ pairs as above.

---

##### Complete Mathematical Model

$$
\begin{align*}
\min\ & \sum_{w \in W_{active}} \sum_{p \in P_{eligible}(w)} c_{w,p} x_{w,p} \\
\text{s.t.}\quad
& \sum_{w \in W_{eligible}(p)} x_{w,p} = 1 \quad \forall p \in P \\
& \sum_{p \in P_{eligible}(w)} x_{w,p} \leq 1 \quad \forall w \in W_{active} \\
& x_{w,p} = 0 \text{ if } (w \text{ on leave}) \vee (\text{skill}(w) < \text{required\_skill}(p)) \vee (c_{w,p} \text{ blank}) \\
& x_{w,p} \in \{0,1\} \quad \forall w,p
\end{align*}
$$

All costs $c_{w,p}$ are in USD cents.

---

##### All required parameters (full vectors/matrices):

- Workers (eligible): W12, W06, W04, W11, W10, W02, W00
- Projects: P00, P01, P02, P03, P04, P05
- Skills and required_skills as above
- Cost matrix as above (with blanks forbidden)
- Skill hierarchy: Junior < Intermediate < Senior < Expert

